# Copy to spikes/.env and fill in what you have. Missing keys never fail a spike: it prints
# "SKIP <spike>: missing KEY1, KEY2" and exits 0. spikes/.env is gitignored. Never paste live-mode keys.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Stripe (SP1, SP4)
# Sandbox only (stripe-best-practices: use a sandbox, not the shared test mode; `stripe sandbox create` works with no account).
# Dashboard > Developers > API keys > Create restricted key (rk_test_...). Least privilege for SP1 + SP4:
#   PaymentIntents: Write, PaymentMethodConfigurations: Read, Account: Read. Nothing else.
#   If a call returns 403, the error names the missing permission; add only that one.
# Never use an sk_ secret key (the scripts refuse anything that is not rk_test_).
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# Dashboard > Developers > API keys > Publishable key (pk_test_...). Only the manual SP4 TWINT page needs it. No permissions to scope.
STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Neon Postgres (SP2, SP3, SP6 optional, SP7)
# Use a throwaway branch of the Frankfurt project (aws-eu-central-1), never the production branch:
#   neon branches create --name sp-spikes --parent main --expires-at <+7 days>   (neon-postgres-branches skill)
# Neon console > Connect > pick that branch. Direct = host WITHOUT "-pooler"; pooled = host WITH "-pooler".
# Role: a role that may CREATE SCHEMA and TABLE on the spike branch. The scripts only touch schemas sp2_spike and sp3_spike and drop them at the end.
# Pooled connection string. Request handlers and SP3 hold requests use it (PgBouncer, transaction mode). SP7 runs the app with the DML-only role here.
DATABASE_URL_POOLED=
# Direct connection string. pg-boss, migrations and SP2 use it (no PgBouncer: needs session state and LISTEN/NOTIFY).
DATABASE_URL_DIRECT=
# SP7 only. Direct string for the DDL role that the Fly release command uses to run Drizzle migrations. The app itself must not hold this role.
DATABASE_URL_DDL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Fly.io (SP3 remote, SP7)
# SP3 must run from a Fly fra machine. Fly sets FLY_REGION on its machines itself: do not paste it here. Leave empty locally.
FLY_REGION=
# Optional: set to 1 to run SP3's Neon part from a laptop. Correctness is checked, but the latency is then not a valid SP3 result.
SP3_ALLOW_NON_FLY=
# SP7. App-scoped deploy token for the staging app only: `fly tokens create deploy -a <staging-app>`. Do not use a personal or org token.
FLY_API_TOKEN=
# SP7. Name of an empty staging Fly app in region fra (`fly apps create`). Scripts deploy only to this app.
FLY_APP_STAGING=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Neon Object Storage (SP5)
# Neon console > Storage (or `neon env pull` after `neon deploy` declares the buckets). Branch credential, Frankfurt project only.
# These four are the AWS-standard names the Neon docs inject. The credential is scoped to one branch: use the spike branch.
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# Branch S3 endpoint, e.g. https://<branch-endpoint>. Path-style addressing is forced by the script.
AWS_ENDPOINT_URL_S3=
# Must be eu-central-1 for the D14 / SP5 pass condition.
AWS_REGION=
# Two buckets declared in neon.ts: one private, one access: "public_read". The defaults below apply when left empty.
SP5_BUCKET_PRIVATE=
SP5_BUCKET_PUBLIC=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Neon Auth (SP6)
# Neon console > Auth > Configuration > Auth URL (includes its path, e.g. https://ep-xxx.neon.tech/neondb/auth). Read-only value.
NEON_AUTH_URL=
# A JWT copied from the SPA after signing in: in the browser console run `(await authClient.token()).data.token`. Valid 15 minutes, so run SP6 right away.
SP6_JWT=
# Optional: a second JWT for the same user fetched at least 16 minutes (or a day) later, to prove renewal.
SP6_JWT_LATER=
